   "evidence": "ZeroCount.lean:106-111 handles `B < 0` via `h.isConst hf (hAB.trans hB)` and `MeromorphicOn.divisor_const`. In ZeroSummability, `hp` is used only to choose `B := (max A 0 + p)/2 < p` and to supply `0 \u2264 p` to the private helper, and both are needed only when `p > 0`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Analysis/Complex/GrowthOrder/ZeroSummability.lean",
   "fix": "Drop `hp` so the signature reads `(h : OrderLE f A) (hf : Differentiable \u2102 f) (hf0 : f 0 \u2260 0) (hAp : A < p)`. Split on `0 < p`; in the `p \u2264 0` case rewrite `f = fun _ \u21a6 f 0`, use `MeromorphicOn.divisor_const` to get an empty support, and conclude summability over the empty index type.",
   "issue": "`hp : 0 < p` in `OrderLE.summable_divisor_mul_norm_rpow` is superfluous: if `p \u2264 0` then `A < p` gives `A < 0`, so `f` is constant and nonzero by `OrderLE.isConst`, the divisor support is empty, and the family is trivially summable. The sibling `isBigO_sum_divisor` already removes the analogous sign condition on `B`.",
   "line": 136
